{
  "case_id": "2009-08-240",
  "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Shell Oil Products Company, LLC",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress enacted the PMPA to regulate two specific, but important, actions: Franchisors' termination of the franchise prior to the conclusion of the franchise term and the franchisors\u2019 non-renewal of the franchise relationship at the end of the agreement's term."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Mr. Lamken, am I wrong that you don't really object to the recognition of \u201cconstructive termination,\u201d if that phrase is used the way it is used elsewhere in contract law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is -- is leaving the premises the sine quo non of a termination?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Your position is that the franchisor has to be the one to terminate?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: When would you -- when would you measure your constructive termination? At what point would the statute of limitations begin to run or stop under your definition?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0000-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. O'NEIL: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The government agrees with Shell that, because there was no termination or non-renewal in any meaningful sense of the word, the dealers failed to state a claim under the PMPA. But, Justice Ginsburg, you are correct: The government parts company with Shell about what the term -- word \"termination,\" does cover. Shell would limit the --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: And what about the statutory right for a preliminary injunction? When would that right kick in, in this situation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Shell",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. O'NEIL: Justice Scalia, we -- we agree with Shell on this. The statute defines \"franchise\" by three elements: The supply of fuel, the use of the leased premises, and the use of the trademark. So someone who is still on a gas station premises that had the Shell sign above them but that had no fuel would not be operating a gas station franchise, and that would be a termination even if the franchisee did not actually pick up and leave the premises. So we would call that a termination."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. O'Neil, I thought that there were some cases, landlord-tenant cases, where the tenant is not required to leave the premises because, as awful as the situation is, the tenant has no place to go."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Shell",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FARRAHER: We do have a test, Your Honor, and the test is whether or not the conduct has effectively eliminated an essential component of one of the three elements of the franchise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What does that mean, \"effectively eliminated\"? The -- the First Circuit said, if \"the breach of the lease was such a material change that it effectively ended the lease, even though the plaintiffs continued to operate the business\" -- I have no idea what that means."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Dealers",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that the injunction is a form of a relief to protect the franchisee, to maintain the status quo. But the existence of a claim under the statute does not depend upon whether or not the franchisee seeks the injunction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can you explain to me -- the question I brought up before -- what was the difference of the elements between the recovery that the jury gave for constructive termination and for breach of contract?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My question is a practical question: What's the harm of sticking to the clear line that is normally there in other cases, in this case not depriving your client of a remedy at all?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Dealers",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I disagree with the Court that the client is not being deprived of a remedy. The remedy available in the statute in one part is injunctive relief. And while the dealers did not avail themselves of that in this particular case, the lesser standard and the lack of a need to show irreparable harm protects the franchisee under a Federal cause of action as distinguished from a contractual-based cause of action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Dealers",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The next question then would be whether or not the dealer must seek injunctive relief as a prerequisite to maintaining a claim, and we argue that there is nothing in the language of the statute suggesting that the injunction is mandatory."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ac3c5524336-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, can I ask you, have you accepted the majority's reasoning in the Dersch case, the Seventh Circuit case, with respect to 2805(f)? You haven't raised that argument in your brief, so obviously, you have accepted their view that 2805(f) doesn't apply to the right to preserve your claims of improper --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-240",
      "confidence": 0.0,
